    "availability": {
      "en": "It goes around the wire, so the circuit never knows it is there — solve the same bench with the clamp on and every number is identical to the digit. What it costs instead is resolution: a hundred-amp jaw reads in ten-milliamp steps and sees nothing at all below fifty, so on a milliamp branch it is the wrong instrument and says so by showing nothing."
    }
